DATA LICENSE NOTICE

The MIT license above covers the SOURCE CODE in this repository and NOTHING
ELSE. It grants no rights in any data, in any model, or in the Sciweon name.
A permissive code license does not make the data permissive.

Data rights are qualified PER SOURCE and PER FIELD, not per dataset. Two
fields in the same record can carry different obligations. The classes:

  FIELD-QUALIFIED PUBLIC
    PubChem (NIH NCBI), PubChem BioAssay
      Public-domain status applies per field, NOT to the resource as a whole.
      NCBI states it "has no rights to transfer to a third party" for
      contributed content, and depositor-provided fields may carry their own
      terms. No unconditional clean-commercial grant is asserted or implied.
    ClinicalTrials.gov, openFDA (US FDA)
      US federal works. Sponsor-contributed free text within a record is not
      necessarily US-government-authored; treat it separately.

  SHARE-ALIKE
    ChEMBL (EMBL-EBI) -- Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 3.0 Unported.
      Attribution AND share-alike attach to any distributed derivative. Note
      that CC BY-SA 3.0 Unported grants no sui generis database right; the
      EU/UK database right in the underlying database is NOT licensed by it.

  ATTRIBUTION REQUIRED, NO LICENSE GRANTED
    PubMed / MEDLINE / RxNorm (NLM)
      NLM asserts contractual acknowledgement, not a copyright license.
      Republishers must additionally state, clearly and conspicuously, when
      the data does not reflect the most current NLM data.
    OpenAlex (OurResearch) -- CC0 for the metadata. Reconstructed abstracts
      are excluded pending confirmation of publisher rights.

  WITHHELD -- not served, not redistributed
    UniProt, UniChem, MedDRA, KEGG, Semantic Scholar, DrugBank-proprietary,
    UMLS `cui` (universally withheld across all UMLS vocabularies).
    Withholding is emitted as an explicit machine-readable state on the API:
    a withheld field is reported as withheld, never silently dropped.

  UNVERIFIED -- treated as restricted until confirmed
    Retraction Watch, EU CTIS (EMA) document reuse terms.
    Prior versions of this notice asserted specific licenses for these
    sources; those assertions were not supported by current primary evidence
    and have been withdrawn rather than restated.

Consumers must comply with the most restrictive applicable upstream terms for
the SPECIFIC FIELDS they use. Entity records carry provenance naming the
originating source; check those before any redistribution or commercial use.

Sciweon makes no warranty regarding upstream data accuracy or completeness.
Original-source errors, retractions and corrections may not be reflected in
any given snapshot. Every API response carries the identity of the snapshot
it was served from; no refresh cadence is promised.

RESEARCH USE ONLY. Sciweon reports observed records with provenance. It does
not assess causality, risk or clinical significance, and makes no clinical,
diagnostic, dosing or regulatory recommendation.
